\par
\b Outcome of your grievance dated 3 May 2023\b0\par
\par
Thank you for attending the grievance meeting on 16 May 2023, accompanied by Jaswinder Sandhu. I have now interviewed Karen Holt and reviewed the maintenance and inspection records for FLT 3. I have considered each of your complaints in turn.\par
\par
\b 1. Removal from Saturday overtime \endash  upheld.\b0  I found no documented operational reason for the change, and it was made three days after you took FLT 3 out of use. You will be restored to the Saturday overtime rota with effect from Saturday 10 June 2023, and you will be paid for the Saturday shifts you missed since 22 April 2023.\par
\par
\b 2. Safety of FLT 3 \endash  upheld.\b0  The independent examination on 22 May 2023 found that the brakes were dangerous. You were right to take the truck out of use. FLT 3 will stay out of service until it has been repaired and re-examined, and all shift managers will be reminded that a tagged-out vehicle must not be returned to use without a maintenance sign-off.\par
\par
\b 3. Comments made by Karen Holt \endash  not upheld.\b0  Ms Holt accepts she told you not to be \ldblquote dramatic\rdblquote  but denies the other comment. As the accounts differ I cannot make a finding, although I have reminded Ms Holt of the company\rquote s Dignity at Work policy.\par
\par
If you are unhappy with this outcome you may appeal in writing to the Operations Director, Mr Neil Garside, within 5 working days of receiving this letter, i.e. by 9 June 2023.\par
\par
Yours sincerely,\par
\par
Michelle Byrne\par
HR Business Partner\par
